# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback — every path served by index.html.
#
# There is deliberately NO server-side "/ -> /public" rule here. One would
# break magic-link sign-in: the link lands on the site root carrying the
# session in the URL, the server redirects it to /public, and the user ends up
# on the public page instead of their dashboard. The token rides in the URL
# *fragment*, which never reaches the server, so no _redirects rule can tell an
# auth landing from a normal visit. Root decides client-side in AuthGuard:
# session -> dashboard, no session -> /public.
/*    /index.html   200
